&lt;p&gt;As 2025 draws to a close, I’m also taking a moment to reflect on the books that I have read this year. It’s been a diverse reading experience, spanning contemporary fiction to analyses of technology and history. I also read a LOT of books about &lt;em&gt;Star Trek&lt;/em&gt; for my work, PhD theses for examination/supervision, and other books that didn’t make this list of “reading for fun”.&lt;/p&gt;

