&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;Journal Articles&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://eprints.bbk.ac.uk/id/eprint/28029&quot; class=&quot;csl-entry&quot;&gt;Eve, Martin Paul, ‘Textual Scholarship and Contemporary Literature: Jennifer Egan’s Editorial Processes and the Archival Edition of &lt;i&gt;Emerald City&lt;/i&gt;’, &lt;i&gt;LIT: Literature, Interpretation, Theory&lt;/i&gt;, 2020&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.16995/cg.158&quot; class=&quot;csl-entry&quot;&gt;McGovern, Melanie, and Martin Paul Eve, ‘Information Labour and Shame in Farmer and Chevli’s &lt;i&gt;Abortion Eve&lt;/i&gt;’, &lt;i&gt;The Comics Grid: Journal of Comics Scholarship&lt;/i&gt;, 9.1 (2019), 6.1-6.28&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.1080/00111619.2019.1568960&quot; class=&quot;csl-entry&quot;&gt;Eve, Martin Paul, ‘Reading Redaction: Symptomatic Metadata, Erasure Poetry, and Mark Blacklock’s &lt;i&gt;I’m Jack&lt;/i&gt;’, &lt;i&gt;Critique: Studies In Contemporary Fiction&lt;/i&gt;, 60.3 (2019), 330–41&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;Book Chapters&lt;/h4&gt;
